      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7304825::rubric_card::000::6980db1684"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The as-deposited film is approximately 900 nm thick.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7304825::rubric_card::000::6980db1684"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The as-deposited film has a nanocrystalline BCC solid-solution structure with an average grain size of approximately 18 nm.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7304825::rubric_card::000::6980db1684"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The as-deposited film has relatively poor interfacial adhesion.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7304825::rubric_card::000::6980db1684"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Post-deposition annealing at 300°C improves film adhesion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7304825::rubric_card::000::6980db1684"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Post-deposition annealing at 300°C reduces the coating's surface roughness.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing refines the nanocrystalline BCC grain structure or its surface grain boundaries.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Improved interfacial bonding and grain refinement increase coating hardness.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Increased hardness and adhesion limit plastic flow and spalling during wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing lowers the coating's room-temperature wear rate relative to the as-deposited coating.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Annealing lowers the room-temperature coefficient of friction relative to the as-deposited coating.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At approximately 300°C, tribochemical oxidation produces oxide phases such as CuO.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tribochemically formed oxides at elevated temperature increase the coefficient of friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At approximately 300°C, the coating retains a lower wear rate than a conventional 304 stainless-steel substrate.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Tribological tests are conducted at room temperature and 300°C using a 1 N load and a sliding speed of 0.1 m/s.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7304825::rubric_card::000::6980db1684"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Nanoindentation and nanopillar-compression measurements are used to assess the coating's mechanical response.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7304825::rubric_card::000::6980db1684"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed mechanism should hold for nanocrystalline refractory HEA coatings near 900 nm thickness and 18 nm grain size from room temperature to about 300°C.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7304825::rubric_card::000::6980db1684"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relative contributions of adhesion improvement and grain refinement to wear performance are not quantitatively established.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
